<title>GERMANY: Germany plans to sell its stake in DB Bank in '97.</title>
<headline>Germany plans to sell its stake in DB Bank in '97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government plans to sell its six percent stake in DG Bank which is said to be valued around 500 million marks, German business daily Boersen Zeitung reported in its Friday edition.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the government announced its plans on Thursday and intends to sell its stake in the bank next year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
